{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "End Funding For Military Interventions Overseas and Spend Taxes In The UK.",
        "additional_details": "We think the British public deserves to know, that their hard-earned money, is being spent responsibly and ethically, prioritising peace, stability and prosperity at home. We seek a foreign policy grounded in diplomacy and peace-building, rather than what can be costly and divisive military actions, that may have limited long-term success.\r\n\r\nThe financial burden of war is significant. The UK\u2019s involvement in wars and military operations over the last two decades has cost billions of pounds.",
        "background": "We demand the government end the use of taxpayers\u2019 money to fund military interventions, or providing military support for conflicts abroad. We believe that our taxes should be spent on improving public services, supporting communities and addressing urgent domestic issues rather than war.",
